---
title: "The WhereTo Trips Partner Program: Texas Founding Partners"
description: "Earn 30% of what WhereTo Trips makes on every trip your followers book, for as long as you stay an active partner. No end date, vested from your first booking. Now recruiting Texas Founding Partners."
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "/TexasPartners/"
---
{#- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Texas Founding Partners — the partner flyer as a page of this site.

    Mirrors texas-partner-flyer.pdf (Oct 2026), served at
    /Partners/texas-partner-flyer.pdf, in the flyer's own order:
    offer, Founding vs Standard terms, who we are, what followers get,
    how it works, three steps, then the application, the booking
    calendar and contact.

    Built from the site's own sections rather than as a port of the PDF:
    hero-slider, highlights, feature-split, tile, step-card,
    download-band. They carry this site's mobile behavior already; the
    hero in particular restacks into photo-band-then-copy below 720px,
    which a hand-rolled two-column sheet layout does not.

    Mobile first: every rule here is written for the narrow case and
    widened with min-width queries, because most creators will open this
    from a link in a message.

    The flyer is deliberately simpler than the Sep 2026 pilot page it
    replaced. Gone on purpose: the three-year window (the Founding rate
    has no end date), the five-step list (the flyer has three), and the
    revenue-by-product section.
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -#}

{%- set mailto = "mailto:Chris@WhereToTrips.com?subject=Texas%20Partner%20Pilot" -%}
{#- Every "Book a short call" on the page scrolls to the calendar at the
    bottom (#book-a-call) instead of leaving for Zoho's own page, which
    carries no Pixel and no PostHog. bookingSrc is Zoho Bookings' embed
    view: schedule.wheretotrips.com itself refuses to be framed
    (X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN), /portal-embed is the version that allows
    it. After a booking, Zoho redirects to /TexasPartners/booked/, which is
    where the "booked" event fires. -#}
{%- set booking = "#book-a-call" -%}
{%- set bookingSrc = "https://schedule.wheretotrips.com/portal-embed#/wheretotrips" -%}
{%- set flyer = "/Partners/texas-partner-flyer.pdf" -%}

{#- The flyer's copy for the four ways in. The photos and links come from
    appModes.json; the one-line descriptions are the flyer's own wording.
    Looked up by key with an inline loop: Nunjucks scopes `set` to the loop
    body, so a match cannot be hoisted out to a variable. -#}
{%- set modeOrder = ["discover", "explore", "together", "direct"] -%}
{%- set wayCopy = {
  "discover": "No destination in mind? A budget, a week off and a vibe are enough.",
  "explore": "Pick a region and see your best matches inside it.",
  "together": "Group trips made simple. Pool your vibes, then vote.",
  "direct": "Already know where you're going? We'll keep it on budget."
} -%}

<style>
  /* ═════ Texas Founding Partners ═════════════════════════════════════
     Page-scoped. This is one outreach page's layout, not a section type
     anything else composes from, so it does not belong in styles.css
     where every other page would download it.

     Written narrow-first; min-width queries widen it. Overrides of
     shared classes (.highlights, .step-card) are class-on-class, which
     outranks styles.css's own max-width queries — so every responsive
     step those classes need is restated here rather than inherited. */

  /* ── Hero photo ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     The wide file has extra sky and sea added on its left, so the subject
     sits right of center and the headline lands on open water and sky. On
     the stacked phone hero the band is nearly square, so the photo is
     aligned to its right edge, which puts her in the middle of the crop. */
  .tp-hero-bg {
    background-image: url('/media/partners/texas-partner-main-1200.jpg');
    background-position: 100% 38%;
  }
  @media (min-width: 721px) {
    .tp-hero-bg {
      background-image: url('/media/partners/texas-partner-main.jpg');
      background-position: center 38%;
    }
  }

  /* ── Offer bar over the hero ──────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-hl { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .tp-hl .highlight-text h4 {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 34px; color: var(--amber);
    line-height: 1; margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  /* Every percent sign on the page is a superscript, set in the face of the
     number it follows. Raised with position rather than vertical-align so it
     never changes the line's height. The text variant is larger because at
     body sizes a half-size sign is too small to read. */
  .tp-pct {
    font-size: .5em; line-height: 0; position: relative; top: -0.78em;
    margin-left: .06em; font-weight: inherit; font-style: normal; letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  .tp-pct--text { font-size: .68em; top: -0.42em; margin-left: .04em; }
  .tp-hl .highlight-text p { font-size: 13.5px; }
  .tp-hl .highlight-text p strong { color: var(--navy); }

  /* ── Hero, wide screens only ──────────────────────────────────────────
     Every rule here is inside min-width:721px on purpose. This <style>
     block comes after styles.css, so an unscoped .hero-slider or
     .slide-caption h1 rule would also beat the shared max-width:720px
     mobile rules and undo the stacked phone hero. */
  @media (min-width: 721px) {
    /* The home page's full-viewport hero is a front door. This is a page
       someone was sent to read, so it opens shorter. */
    .hero-slider { height: clamp(520px, 74vh, 700px); }
    /* Wide enough that each sentence of the headline holds one line. */
    .slide-caption { max-width: 880px; }
    .slide-caption h1 { font-size: clamp(34px, 4.3vw, 54px); }
    .sec-head { max-width: 820px; }
    /* The shared wash clears by 68% of the width. This page's headline runs
       wider than the home page's, so it carries further before fading. */
    .hero-slide-overlay {
      background:
        linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(25,25,25,0.76) 0%, rgba(25,25,25,0.56) 42%,
                               rgba(25,25,25,0.24) 64%, rgba(25,25,25,0) 78%),
        linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(25,25,25,0.5) 0%, transparent 45%);
    }
  }

  /* The shared rule caps the photo-overlaid eyebrow at 70% of the width,
     which wraps this page's longer one and strands the separator. */
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .slide-eyebrow { max-width: 94%; } }

  /* ── Founding vs Standard ─────────────────────────────────────────────
     Narrow: each row is its label, then the two rates side by side under
     the two column heads. Wide: the flyer's three-column table. */
  .tp-compare {
    border: 1px solid var(--wg200); border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden; background: var(--card);
  }
  .tp-cmp-head, .tp-cmp-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  .tp-cmp-head > span {
    padding: 11px 14px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted); background: var(--tint);
  }
  .tp-cmp-head > .tp-cmp-blank { display: none; }
  .tp-cmp-head > .is-founding { background: var(--amber); color: #fff; }
  .tp-cmp-row { border-top: 1px solid var(--wg200); }
  .tp-cmp-label {
    grid-column: 1 / -1; padding: 12px 14px 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .tp-cmp-cell { padding: 4px 14px 14px; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.4; }
  .tp-cmp-cell.is-founding { background: var(--amber-tint); color: var(--navy); font-weight: 700; }
  .tp-cmp-rate { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 26px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.1; }
  .tp-cmp-cell.is-founding.tp-cmp-rate { color: var(--amber-deep); }
  .tp-ask { margin-top: 18px; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .tp-ask strong { color: var(--navy); }
  .tp-cta-band { margin-top: clamp(28px, 5vw, 44px); }
  .tp-cta-band .btn { margin-top: 6px; }
  @media (min-width: 721px) {
    .tp-cmp-head, .tp-cmp-row { grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1.4fr 1.4fr; }
    .tp-cmp-head > .tp-cmp-blank { display: block; }
    .tp-cmp-head > span { padding: 13px 20px; }
    .tp-cmp-label { grid-column: auto; padding: 18px 20px; font-size: 14px; align-self: center; }
    .tp-cmp-cell { padding: 18px 20px; font-size: 15.5px; align-self: center; }
    .tp-cmp-rate { font-size: 30px; }
  }

  /* ── Vibe Engine: the worked example ──────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-example { margin-top: 28px; }
  .tp-example-label {
    font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted);
    display: block; margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .tp-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .tp-chip-result {
    background: var(--amber-tint); border-color: var(--amber);
    color: var(--amber-deep); font-weight: 600; cursor: default;
  }
  .tp-chip-result:hover {
    background: var(--amber); color: #fff; border-color: var(--amber);
  }
  .tp-chip-budget { background: var(--azure-tint); border-color: var(--azure); color: var(--azure); font-weight: 700; }

  .feature-img.tp-phone { height: clamp(220px, 46vw, 300px); }
  @media (min-width: 961px) { .feature-img.tp-phone { height: clamp(300px, 30vw, 420px); } }

  /* ── Card grids ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-ways { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 14px; }
  .tp-ways .tile { padding: 12px 12px 18px; }
  .tp-ways .tile-img { height: 104px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .tp-ways h3 { font-size: 17px; }
  .tp-ways p { font-size: 13px; }

  .tp-benefits { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 14px; }

  /* ── Three steps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 14px; }
  .tp-note {
    margin-top: 22px; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  /* ── Book a short call ────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Phones: intro, then the calendar, then the details, so the calendar is
     what a "Book a short call" tap lands next to. Wider: intro and details
     stack on the left, the calendar on the right. */
  .tp-book { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 26px; grid-template-areas: "intro" "cal" "details"; }
  .tp-book-intro { grid-area: intro; } .tp-cal-col { grid-area: cal; } .tp-book-details { grid-area: details; }
  .tp-book-intro h2 { margin: 0; }
  .tp-book-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin: 18px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .tp-book-meta li {
    font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--navy);
    background: var(--azure-tint); border-radius: 999px; padding: 7px 14px;
  }
  .tp-host { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
  .tp-avatar {
    width: 56px; height: 56px; border-radius: 50%; flex: none; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    background: var(--navy); color: #fff; font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 22px; letter-spacing: .02em;
  }
  .tp-host strong { display: block; color: var(--navy); font-size: 16px; }
  .tp-host span { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 14px; }
  .tp-cover { margin: 20px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--wg200); }
  .tp-cover li { padding: 16px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--wg200); }
  .tp-cover h3 { font-size: 19px; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .tp-cover p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; }
  /* The calendar is Zoho's page in a frame. The "loading" line sits behind
     it, so the frame is never an empty white box while Zoho starts up. */
  .tp-cal {
    position: relative; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--wg200); border-radius: 22px;
    overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 24px 50px rgba(20, 40, 60, .08);
  }
  .tp-cal-wait {
    position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 14px;
  }
  .tp-cal iframe { position: relative; display: block; width: 100%; height: 820px; border: 0; background: transparent; }
  .tp-cal-alt { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-muted); text-align: center; }
  .tp-cal-alt a { color: var(--azure); font-weight: 600; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .tp-book {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr); grid-template-areas: "intro cal" "details cal";
      column-gap: 48px; row-gap: 28px; align-items: start;
    }
    .tp-cal-col { position: sticky; top: 110px; }
    .tp-cal iframe { height: 700px; }
  }

  /* ── Closing CTA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-mail-btn { font-size: 15px; text-transform: none; max-width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding-inline: clamp(18px, 5vw, 32px); }
  /* The address is one unbroken line at every width. It is sized to the band it
     sits in (6cqi is about 1/16 of the band's width, and the address is about
     15.7 em long), with a viewport-based size first for any browser without
     container units. nowrap is the guarantee; the sizing keeps it inside. */
  .download-band .tp-email {
    font-size: clamp(13px, calc((100vw - 110px) / 17), 44px);
    white-space: nowrap; overflow-wrap: normal;
    max-width: none;   /* the shared band heading is capped at 18ch, which cuts the address */
  }
  @supports (font-size: 1cqi) {
    .tp-closing-band { container-type: inline-size; }
    .download-band .tp-email { font-size: clamp(13px, 5.9cqi, 44px); }
  }
  .tp-flyer {
    display: inline-block; margin-top: 16px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.86); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .tp-flyer:hover { color: #fff; }
  .tp-fine {
    margin: 30px auto 0; max-width: 62ch; text-align: left;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--amber); padding-left: 16px;
  }
  .tp-fine h4 {
    font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--amber);
    letter-spacing: .04em; margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .tp-fine p { font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.68); margin: 0; max-width: none; }
  .tp-legal {
    font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 96ch; margin: 26px auto 0; text-align: center;
  }

  /* ── Sticky reply bar, phones only ────────────────────────────────────
     The page is long and the one action it asks for sits at the bottom of
     it. The bar appears once the hero has scrolled away and hides again
     over the application so it never covers the form it duplicates. */
  .tp-bar {
    position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; z-index: 60;
    padding: 10px 16px calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.96); backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--wg200); box-shadow: 0 -6px 24px rgba(20,30,40,0.10);
    transform: translateY(110%); transition: transform .28s ease;
  }
  .tp-bar.is-on { transform: none; }
  .tp-bar .btn { box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; justify-content: center; padding: 15px 20px; }
  @media (min-width: 721px) { .tp-bar { display: none; } }

  /* ── Wider screens ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (min-width: 561px) {
    .tp-benefits { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 18px; }
    .tp-steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 18px; }
    .tp-ways { gap: 18px; }
    .tp-ways .tile-img { height: 140px; }
  }
  @media (min-width: 721px) {
    .tp-hl { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
    .tp-hl .highlight-text h4 { font-size: 38px; }
  }
  @media (min-width: 961px) {
    .tp-ways { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 22px; }
    .tp-ways .tile-img { height: 150px; }
    .tp-ways h3 { font-size: 20px; }
    .tp-ways p { font-size: 13.5px; }
    .tp-benefits { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 20px; }
    .tp-steps .step-card { padding: 26px 24px; }
  }
</style>

{# ═══ Hero ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="hero-slider">
  <div class="hero-slides">
    <div class="hero-slide tp-hero-bg active" role="img"
         aria-label="A young woman laughing as she records a video on a phone, on a beach at sunset"></div>
    <div class="hero-slide-overlay"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap hero-caption-wrap">
    <div class="slide-caption">
      <div class="slide-eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow">Now recruiting Texas Founding Partners</span></div>
      <div class="slide-title">
        <h1>Earn 30<span class="tp-pct">%</span> on every trip.
<span class="italic">For as long as you're active.</span></h1>
      </div>
      <div class="slide-subtitle">
        <p class="lede">We're launching in Texas with a small group of Founding Partners. Every time
          one of your followers books a trip on WhereTo, you get 30<span class="tp-pct tp-pct--text">%</span> of what we earn. There's no end
          date. You keep earning as long as you stay an active partner.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="btns">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ booking }}">Book a short call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-hero-ghost" href="#what-you-earn">See the Founding terms</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ The offer, in three numbers ═══════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="highlights-wrap">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="highlights tp-hl reveal">
      <div class="highlight">
        <span class="highlight-icon">{% icon "hand-money" %}</span>
        <div class="highlight-text">
          <h4>30<span class="tp-pct">%</span></h4>
          <p><strong>Revenue share</strong><br>on every completed booking your followers make</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="highlight">
        <span class="highlight-icon">{% icon "infinity" %}</span>
        <div class="highlight-text">
          <h4>No end date</h4>
          <p><strong>Lifetime earnings</strong><br>keep earning as long as you stay active</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="highlight">
        <span class="highlight-icon">{% icon "verified-check" %}</span>
        <div class="highlight-text">
          <h4>100<span class="tp-pct">%</span></h4>
          <p><strong>Vested on day one</strong><br>full Founding rate from your first booking</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ Founding vs Standard ══════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block" id="what-you-earn">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">The Founding terms</span>
      <h2>Founding Partner <span class="italic">vs. Standard.</span></h2>
    </div>

    <div class="tp-compare reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <div class="tp-cmp-head">
        <span class="tp-cmp-blank"></span>
        <span class="is-founding">Founding Partner</span>
        <span>Standard Partner</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tp-cmp-row">
        <span class="tp-cmp-label">Revenue share</span>
        <span class="tp-cmp-cell tp-cmp-rate is-founding">30<span class="tp-pct">%</span></span>
        <span class="tp-cmp-cell tp-cmp-rate">20<span class="tp-pct">%</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="tp-cmp-row">
        <span class="tp-cmp-label">How long you earn</span>
        <span class="tp-cmp-cell is-founding">As long as you're active</span>
        <span class="tp-cmp-cell">First 24 months</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tp-cmp-row">
        <span class="tp-cmp-label">Who qualifies</span>
        <span class="tp-cmp-cell is-founding">Texas launch partners only</span>
        <span class="tp-cmp-cell">Partners who join later</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="tp-ask reveal"><strong>All we ask:</strong> four approved posts a year to stay active,
      prorated in year one.</p>

    <div class="download-band tp-cta-band reveal">
      <h2>Founding spots are limited.</h2>
      <p>Book a short call and we'll walk you through it.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-light tp-mail-btn" href="{{ booking }}">Pick a time</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ Who we are ════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="feature-split">
      <div class="feature-img-wrap reveal">
        <img class="feature-img" src="/media/partners/texas-partner-hero-720.jpg"
             srcset="/media/partners/texas-partner-hero-720.jpg 720w, /media/partners/texas-partner-hero.jpg 1200w"
             sizes="(max-width: 960px) 92vw, 46vw"
             alt="A traveler looking out over a mountain lake" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="feature-text reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <span class="eyebrow">Texas Founding Partners</span>
        <h2>Start with you. End up somewhere <span class="italic">amazing.</span></h2>
        <p class="lede">WhereTo Trips is a Texas-based travel app that helps people figure out where
          to go, plan the trip and book it in one place.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">We're launching in Texas first.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ What your followers get ═══════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block" id="vibe-engine">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="feature-split flip">
      <div class="feature-img-wrap reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <img class="feature-img img-transparent tp-phone" src="/media/oniPhone_2.png"
             alt="The WhereTo app showing a scored destination result" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="feature-text reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">What your followers get</span>
        <h2>Where will your vibes <span class="italic">take you?</span></h2>
        <p class="lede">A traveler tells WhereTo their budget, their dates and the vibes they're
          after. Our Vibe Engine finds destinations that fit and builds a flight and hotel package at
          or under their budget.</p>

        <div class="tp-example">
          <span class="tp-example-label">What a traveler puts in</span>
          <div class="tp-chips">
            <span class="chip tp-chip-budget">$3,400</span>
            <span class="chip">A week in March</span>
            <span class="chip">Food &amp; live music</span>
          </div>
          <span class="tp-example-label" style="margin-top: 18px;">What comes back</span>
          <div class="tp-chips">
            <span class="chip tp-chip-result">Cabo San Lucas, MX</span>
            <span class="chip tp-chip-result">Valparaiso, FL</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tp-ways reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-top: clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px);">
      {% for key in modeOrder %}{% for m in appModes %}{% if m.key == key %}
      {#- New tab: this is an outreach page someone was sent, and a workflow
          page is a detour off it rather than the next step. Losing their
          place on the way back is how they stop reading it. -#}
      <a class="tile" href="{{ m.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <img class="tile-img" src="{{ m.images[0] | thumb(520) }}"
             srcset="{{ m.images[0] | thumbSet([320, 520, 760]) }}"
             sizes="(max-width: 960px) 46vw, 23vw"
             alt="{{ m.title }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <h3>{% if m.key == "together" %}Wander Together{% else %}{{ m.titleAccent }}{% endif %}</h3>
        <p>{{ wayCopy[m.key] }}</p>
      </a>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

