{# ═══ Apply ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   The same form /partners/ uses, by including the same partial
   rather than copying its markup, so a change to partner_application.njk
   reaches both pages at once. Both write into Zoho CRM Leads through
   capture-submission; only the email subject names the pilot, so Chris can
   tell them apart in an inbox. The subject is left as it was so any inbox
   rule or CRM filter keyed on it keeps matching.
   The sticky reply bar hides from here down (data-tp-cta), because from
   here on the thing it links to is already on screen.
   `background` is on: the steps section above is plain, so the form band
   reads as its own block. #}
